config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_EV_CHARGE_CONTROL
	bool "Domoticz plugin: timed EV charger control"
	depends on FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	default n
	help
		Timed charging control for an electric vehicle: the plugin
		switches an existing Domoticz device (the switch or contactor
		that enables the wallbox) ON and OFF according to a schedule
		configured on the hardware page, and it can be disabled
		temporarily without losing the schedule.

		A safety function refuses to switch the charger ON again within
		30 minutes of a switch OFF, which protects the on-board charger
		of the car from being cycled when the schedule is changed or the
		box restarts.

		The controlled device is any Domoticz switch, for example a
		Wi-Fi or Zigbee relay; the plugin only uses the Domoticz module
		and the Python standard library.

		Setup: Setup -> Hardware -> add "EV charger timer" (or similar),
		then select the switch device and the ON/OFF times.

		Licensed MIT upstream (LICENSE is installed with the plugin).
		The repository has no release tags, so the build fetches a
		pinned commit of the main branch.
